  "discussion": "Broadly, the risk management framework used by the [Information Security Manual](https://www.cyber.gov.au/resources-business-and-government/essential-cyber-security/ism) has six steps: define the system, select controls, implement controls, assess controls, authorise the system and monitor the system. System owners are responsible for the implementation of this six-step risk management framework for each of their systems.",
